    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im having some issues with our sublimation heat press line. the colors are coming out really faded and not transferring to the fabric like they should. we checked the settings but they seem right. what should i be looking at for temp and pressure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Faded colors and poor transfer, even with settings seemingly correct, usually point to a few common issues. First, check your pre-press application; if the sublimation ink isn't fully bonded to the transfer paper, it won't adhere to the fabric. You might need to increase the pressure slightly or ensure the heat is fully penetrating the paper. Sometimes, the paper itself is the culprit, perhaps it's not rated for the specific dye or substrate you are using.",
